<title>TUNISIA: Japan's EX-IM Bank to lend 10 bln yen to Tunisia.</title>
<headline>Japan's EX-IM Bank to lend 10 bln yen to Tunisia.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Japan will lend Tunisia 10 billion yen in co-financing with Japanese commercial banks to support the Tunisian private sector, officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said the loan, aimed at helping upgrade Tunisian private fims, included a seven billion yen from the Ex-Im Bank and three billion yen provided by Japanese private banks.</p>
<p>The loan was for a 12-year maturity and two-year period of grace and was at the market's prices, they added.</p>
<p>The agreement was signed over the week end in Tokyo.</p>
</text>
